    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` rule: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nTwo small, focused edits, each in its natural home:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property (enum `BRONZE`/`SILVER`) to the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived read-only fields like `displayName`, `initials`, and `namesakeCount`. This is the single source of truth for the DTO (the `OwnerDto` is generated from it at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the field via a small, single-purpose `membershipTier(Owner)` default method. This sits right next to the existing derived-field logic (`displayName`, `initials`), which is the established place for computed response-only attributes. Because the tier is purely derived (not stored on the entity \u2014 there's no `membership_tier` column), the mapper handles it consistently for both the POST-create response and the GET response, so no pipeline step or entity change was needed.\n\nTests: both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
